Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. VOSS AND VALE'S ROOM - MONDAY - MORNING

Two orders beneath the lamp. A historic contractor copy and an authenticated court copy obtained through an independent solicitor.

Same case, hearing, judge and seal format. Different operative text.

Vale reads the true order: supervised contact continues; temporary placement continues; review in six weeks.

The variant suspends contact, transfers authority and adds a paragraph permitting recovery, transport and relocation. The true order has no paragraph thirteen.

VALE
We verified the wrapper. Not the text.

VOSS
Yes.

VALE
Someone had the real one.

VOSS
Access to a genuine copy. Not proof which person altered it.

INT. DOCUMENT-REVIEW ROOM - SAME DAY

Zoe searches MPS-17-4408 on the working copy. It links another root, H09-55216, to document control: BASE FC-771/12, VARIANT S3, OVR2, VERIFY C2, DELIVERY MPS.

They inspect metadata, not the private source image. Source image first, text extract and seal map, then the variant. Earlier versions remain unknown.

Zoe sends only BASE FC-771/12 / COMPARE TEXT. Voss returns only the operative differences, no child names.

ZOE
The override changes what happens. This makes it look as if a judge ordered it.

C2 reads CONTROLLED VERIFICATION: supplied primary and secondary contacts, escalation back to document control, external registry check discouraged.

At the other table Vale calls the historic supplied line. It still says AUTHENTICATED, but will not name the source court or answer about paragraph thirteen.

The independent source says otherwise.

ZOE
Different doors. Same answer machine.

She draws REAL COURT outside the loop.

EXT. CAFE - AFTERNOON

Over food Zoe lists what they cannot prove: creator, source supplier, knowing Meridian staff, court insider, recipient knowledge, or the same mechanism in her case.

ZOE
Seeing the fake doesn't mean you knew it was fake. No more on that child or her mother.

INT. MAC'S STUDY/CAIN'S HOUSE - INTERCUT

Mac wants the verification line shut. His solicitor warns that closure after comparison exposes significance; the legacy system does not answer to one sponsor.

Cain orders no further box movement. He watches access records and waits for the next question.

INT. HOTEL - NIGHT

Zoe looks at her backpack, then away.

ZOE
Not my order yet. I want the next move to show the system, not just explain me.

She writes THE PROFILE. The real years of her childhood remain real even if their starting authority was false.
